 Therapeutics</source><year>2006</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>576</fpage><lpage>586</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17037972</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1089/dia.2006.8.576</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hess</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Bryce</surname><given-names>CL</given-names></name><name><surname>Paone</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Fischer</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>McTigue</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Olshansky</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Zickmund</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Fitzgerald</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Siminerio</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Exploring challenges and potentials of personal health records in diabetes self-management: implementation and initial assessment</article-title><source>Telemedicine Journal &#x00026; E-Health</source><year>2007</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>509</fpage><lpage>517</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17999613</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1089/tmj.2006.0089</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kho</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Duffett</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Willison</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Cook</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Brouwers</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Written informed consent and selection bias in observational studies using medical records: systematic review</article-title><source>BMJ</source><year>2009</year><volume>338</volume><fpage>b866</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type=